- Should I be referred to cardiology (or electrophysiology) now, or can you manage AF as PCP? If referral is recommended, can you send to Colorado Cardiology or an EP specialist?
- If I have symptoms between visits (palpitations, chest pain, syncope), who should I contact and when should I go to urgent care/ER?
- Are any of my current meds (omeprazole or gabapentin, or my antidepressant if I take one) likely to interact with anticoagulants?
- Are there lifestyle changes (weight, alcohol, sleep apnea treatment) that might reduce AF episodes?

7) Practical next steps for you now
- Please confirm the creatinine result (unit and date). If it truly is extremely high, call your PCP or go to the ER.
