- New or symptomatic AF that needs rhythm-control discussion (especially if symptomatic despite initial therapy).
- Difficulty starting or managing anticoagulation, complex kidney disease, prior thromboembolism, or prior bleeding on anticoagulants.
- Structural heart disease on echo, heart failure, or reduced ejection fraction.
- Recurrent AF despite meds, or if you are considering catheter ablation.
- Unexplained syncope, very rapid ventricular rates, or hemodynamic instability.

