Ask Dr. Wilson to arrange or bring results of:
- Recent basic metabolic panel (BMP) with serum creatinine and calculated eGFR / estimated CrCl
- Hemoglobin / platelet count (for bleeding risk)
- INR if on warfarin
- HbA1c (diabetes control)
- Resting ECG (12-lead)
- 24–48 hour Holter or event monitor if palpitations are intermittent and diagnosis uncertain
- Transthoracic echocardiogram if structural heart disease is suspected or to evaluate function/valves
- TSH (thyroid disease can trigger AF)
- If you already see a cardiologist, bring prior echo/ECG/records

