8) Urgent symptoms — go to ER or call 911 if you have:
- Sudden weakness, slurred speech, facial droop (possible stroke)
- Sudden severe chest pain, crushing pain, or shortness of breath suggesting heart attack or severe heart failure
- Syncope with injury or prolonged unconsciousness
- Very rapid heart rate with dizziness, fainting, or low blood pressure

