Key background to know (short)
- Stroke risk in AF is estimated with CHADS‑VASc (congestive heart failure, hypertension, age ≥75, diabetes, stroke/TIA prior, vascular disease, age 65–74, female sex). Diabetes gives 1 point; age 55 does not add a point. If your CHADS‑VASc meets treatment thresholds, anticoagulation is generally recommended.
