- Any prior ECGs, Holter/ambulatory monitor reports, and echocardiogram reports.
- History of stroke/TIA, major bleeding, falls, or GI bleeding.
- Blood pressure readings, alcohol use, and adherence to diabetes medications.
- Symptoms: palpitations, shortness of breath, chest pain, lightheadedness, fatigue — when they started and how often.
- If you’re on an antidepressant or an SSRI/SNRI: these can increase bleeding risk when combined with anticoagulants — list exact drug/dose.

