- Do I have documented atrial fibrillation? If so, what type (paroxysmal/persistent/permanent)?
- Based on my history and scores, do I need anticoagulation to prevent stroke? Which score (CHA2DS2‑VASc) do I have?
- If anticoagulation is recommended, which agent do you prefer for me (apixaban, rivaroxaban, dabigatran, warfarin) and why — especially given my renal function?
- Are there any interactions with my current meds (omeprazole, gabapentin, and any antidepressant) that would change anticoagulant choice?
- Do you recommend an echocardiogram, longer rhythm monitoring (e.g., 24–48 hr Holter or event monitor), or labs before starting/changing anticoagulation?
