- ECG (12‑lead) to document rhythm.
- Ambulatory rhythm monitoring if symptoms are intermittent (Holter, event monitor, or implantable loop recorder as appropriate).
- Transthoracic echocardiogram (TTE) to check heart structure/function.
- CBC (to check baseline hemoglobin/platelets), LFTs, coagulation if on warfarin (INR).
- Sleep apnea screen if relevant (OSA is an AF risk factor).
- History of prior stroke/TIA, bleeding, falls, or GI bleeds.

4) When to consider referral to cardiology (Colorado Cardiology)
Consider asking Dr. Wilson for a cardiology referral if any of the following apply:
