- If you take antidepressants (SSRIs/SNRIs), they can increase bleeding risk when combined with anticoagulants; this is important to discuss.  
- Warfarin requires INR monitoring and has many interactions (diet and drugs). DOACs have fewer interactions but require dose adjustments for renal function and interact with strong P-gp/CYP3A inhibitors.  
- Ask your clinician to review all meds for interactions before prescribing anticoagulation.

